  "answer": "I couldn't find a past ticket that matches this problem. The archive has many older reports of the PowerToys Settings window not opening while the modules keep working. Those had different causes: an old Windows build (#3881), a broken .NET runtime (#13202), and Settings only working after a restart as admin (#18889). Your ticket has no steps, no error text and no actual-behavior description, and I can't open the bug report ZIP, so I can't tell which of these applies, if any. Please try the following. 1) Fully exit PowerToys from the tray, then start it again and open Settings. 2) Try right-clicking the tray icon and choosing 'Restart as administrator'. 3) Update to the latest PowerToys from the Store, or repair or reinstall it. 4) Check Event Viewer > Windows Logs > Application for PowerToys.Settings.exe errors. 5) Reply with what happens when you click Settings (nothing, a blank window, or an error), your Windows version, and a fresh bug report. With those details we can look for a closer match."
 },
